~ start
Guide: Oh hey, you made it. Welcome to the Edge of the Feed. I'm Sage. Your local guide, part chill friend, part "I might've scrolled too long again last night."
Guide: So uh... before we jump in... quick question: Did you ever open social media and immediately feel like your entire life is... not aesthetic enough?
- Literally every day.
    => highlight_reel
- Sometimes.
    => highlight_reel
- Nah, I'm built different.
    => highlight_reel
- I refuse to answer that.
    => highlight_reel

~ highlight_reel
Guide: Honestly? Same. My feed looks like this magical land where everyone else is glowing and productive while I'm over here eating cereal for dinner. Twice.
Guide: But here's the secret the apps don't tell you... Everything you're seeing? Yeah, that's a highlight reel. Like, the top 1% moments of someone's life.
Guide: Meanwhile you're comparing it to your entire behind-the-scenes. The messy hair. The stress. The "Wait, what am I even doing today?" vibes.
Guide: Let me ask you something though. When you see someone posting their dream vacation or perfect gym pic... what does your brain do?
- Glad for them!
    => comparison_trap
- Immediately compare myself.
    => comparison_trap
- I KNOW it's curated but my brain still attacks me.
    => comparison_trap
- Uninstalling the app as we speak.
    => comparison_trap

~ comparison_trap
Guide: All totally normal. Your brain is literally built to compare itself to others. It's trying to figure out where you fit socially — which is cool and all — BUT social media turns that instinct into a full-time job.
Guide: Instead of comparing yourself to a few people, suddenly you're comparing yourself to thousands of edited, filtered, perfectly lit moments every single day. And your brain's like, "Oh wow... everyone else has their life together."
Guide: Spoiler: they don't.
=> END